        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Greenworks makes a snow machine for nearly every driveway, which is exactly why the choice deserves a minute of thought. Start with the batteries you already own, then match the class to your snow: a power shovel for steps and walks, a single-stage for paved drives under eight inches, and the 24-inch two-stage only when gravel, depth, distance or a plow berm demand it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Read the specific listing before you buy, because kits, batteries and listed specs vary by SKU and retailer. Compare total amp-hours rather than sticker price, keep the packs warm, and the right Greenworks will clear your driveway for a lot less than a premium-brand machine.
          </p>
